WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.600
I want to tell you about a player who

00:01.680 --> 00:03.600
got on a plane to England for a tryout.

00:04.000 --> 00:04.800
The club saw him.

00:05.240 --> 00:05.840
They loved him.

00:06.280 --> 00:07.360
They wanted to sign him.

00:07.880 --> 00:08.400
And they couldn't.

00:09.040 --> 00:10.240
Not because he wasn't good enough.

00:10.840 --> 00:12.560
Because the club had already used up

00:12.640 --> 00:14.320
every one of its work permit slots for

00:14.400 --> 00:15.520
foreign players that season.

00:16.160 --> 00:17.760
Nobody had checked before booking the

00:17.920 --> 00:18.080
flight.

00:18.680 --> 00:21.120
An entire trip, an entire opportunity,

00:21.680 --> 00:23.680
gone, because somebody skipped a step

00:23.760 --> 00:25.360
that takes ten minutes of research.

00:26.040 --> 00:28.400
I'm Bert Mahecha, founder of MFH Global

00:28.480 --> 00:30.560
Football, and I tell that story because

00:30.600 --> 00:32.720
it's the clearest example I know of why

00:32.760 --> 00:34.800
the regulatory side of this job matters

00:34.880 --> 00:36.240
as much as the football side.

00:36.880 --> 00:38.720
A lot of agents focus entirely on

00:38.800 --> 00:40.160
getting a player in front of a club.

00:40.840 --> 00:42.480
Almost none of them ask the questions

00:42.560 --> 00:44.000
that determine whether a deal can

00:44.240 --> 00:46.160
actually happen once the club says yes.

00:46.720 --> 00:48.560
Before I ever put a player on a plane,

00:48.840 --> 00:50.640
I'm checking things most families never

00:50.720 --> 00:51.200
hear about.

00:51.760 --> 00:53.360
Does this country's foreign player quota

00:53.440 --> 00:54.640
have room left this season.

00:55.200 --> 00:56.800
Does this player qualify for a work

00:56.880 --> 00:58.480
permit based on his nationality and

00:58.560 --> 00:59.280
playing history.

00:59.920 --> 01:02.000
Is this even inside an open transfer

01:02.160 --> 01:03.760
window, because there are only three of

01:03.840 --> 01:05.840
those a year, and missing one can mean

01:06.000 --> 01:07.280
waiting months for the next.

01:07.840 --> 01:09.200
These aren't small details.

01:09.600 --> 01:10.640
They're the difference between an

01:10.720 --> 01:12.560
opportunity and a wasted trip.

01:13.200 --> 01:14.400
This is what I mean when I say the

01:14.480 --> 01:16.480
player's future always comes first.

01:16.960 --> 01:18.080
It's not just a phrase.

01:18.560 --> 01:20.640
It means doing the homework nobody sees,

01:20.960 --> 01:22.480
so that when a real opportunity shows

01:22.560 --> 01:24.720
up, it can actually become a contract,

01:25.040 --> 01:26.720
instead of becoming a story about what

01:26.920 --> 01:27.600
almost happened.

01:28.240 --> 01:30.080
I can't promise every deal closes.

01:30.480 --> 01:32.000
Nobody honest can promise that.

01:32.480 --> 01:34.400
What I can promise is that I'll ask the

01:34.480 --> 01:36.080
questions that matter before you ever

01:36.160 --> 01:38.640
pack a bag, so your family's time, and

01:38.680 --> 01:40.640
your child's shot, aren't wasted on a

01:40.720 --> 01:42.240
trip that was never going to work.

01:42.880 --> 01:44.640
If you're a transfer ready player, or a

01:44.720 --> 01:46.080
family trying to understand what

01:46.160 --> 01:47.760
actually goes into a move like this,

01:48.240 --> 01:49.360
book a free consultation.

01:49.840 --> 01:51.600
Let's make sure your next opportunity is

01:51.680 --> 01:52.240
a real one.
